 0.0213623046875, 0.0084991455078125, -0.00653076171875, 0.0296783447265625, -0.036895751953125, 0.01513671875, 0.0085906982421875, -0.00319671630859375, 0.02099609375, -0.002330780029296875, 0.040618896484375, -0.0014085769653320312, 0.053436279296875, 0.004505157470703125, 0.0413818359375, -0.0065155029296875, -0.0017728805541992188, 0.0017004013061523438, -0.016937255859375, 0.00675201416015625, -0.00036144256591796875, -0.022247314453125, 0.023406982421875, 0.0498046875, -0.019256591796875, -0.0181884765625, -0.030975341796875, 0.02337646484375, -0.0205841064453125, 0.00315093994140625, 0.046722412109375, 0.03466796875, 0.001739501953125, -0.03240966796875, -0.01183319091796875, -0.01016998291015625, 0.00952911376953125, -0.027740478515625, 0.015869140625, -0.0167236328125, -0.02154541015625, -0.01227569580078125, -0.01079559326171875, 0.03240966796875, 0.00992584228515625, -0.01122283935546875, -0.00826263427734375], "payload": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "text": "Large-scale image generation has progressed through advances in data scale, quality, rebalancing, and recaptioning. However, conventional pipelines typically optimize task-specific datasets independently. The main challenge lies not only in curating each task-specific corpus, but also in organizing heterogeneous supervision according to the dependencies among generative capabilities. We propose a \\textbf{capability-driven data infrastructure} that unifies capability-specific supervision construction with capability-aligned curriculum scheduling. This infrastructure consists of three specialized yet interoperable data engines, each delivering complementary relational supervision for text-image grounding, inter-image transformation, and image-knowledge association. Caption experts further align text-to-image (T2I) and editing supervision across tasks and levels of granularity. A multi-stage curriculum jointly evolves task composition, visual concept distribution, data quality, and image resolution in accordance with the dependency order of capability acquisition. Capability-aware evaluation closes the loop through targeted retrieval, expert construction, and gap-aware resampling. At scale, this framework curates a 440M-image T2I corpus, 120M editing pairs, and over 27M image-entity pairs. Using this infrastructure, we train multimodal diffusion models from scratch at two scales, with 3B and 6B parameters, respectively. We conduct quantitative evaluation on CPI-Bench, as well as qualitative assessments across diverse text-to-image and editing scenarios. Experimental results demonstrate broad visual coverage, versatile rendering, and effective transfer across generative capabilities."}}